<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108318" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόδῐκος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>brought to trial</i> or <i>liable to be tried,</i>
			Lex ap. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				10.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				954a
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHal.</u>
				1.72
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐχ
				ὑ. [ἐστι] τὰ εἰκότα</span> not <i>liable to action,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1376a22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i>for</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. γενέσθαι χερῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					260
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδραποδισμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					879a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδενὸς τούτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					4.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς κακώσεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					8.32
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδ</span>- codd.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					54.25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ βλάβους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PHal.</u>
					1.101
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>: with the person injured in dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τῷ παθόντι</span> Lex ap.<i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τῷ ἐθέλοντι τιμωρεῖν γιγνέσθω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					871b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν διπλασίων ὑ. ἔστω τῷ
				βλαφθέντι</span> let him be <i>liable to forfeit</i> twice
			the amount to the person damaged, ib.<i><span class="en">
				846b
			</span></i> (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ποτὶ διπλοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(1).1390.78
				</span></i>
			 (Andania, <span class="entity">i B. C.</span>)); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ἀσεβείας γιγνέσθω τῷ ἐθέλοντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					868d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα ὑ. γένηται πᾶς ὁ κόσμος τῷ
					θεῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
					3.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
